# Other colliding columns are renamed `name1`, … with one DS1007 info per join.
mode: check
show: schema
schema: 'orders.csv'(orderId: string, customerId: string, amount: real, qty: long, timestamp: datetime); 'r.csv'(customerId: string, amount: real, qty: long, qty1: long)
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | join 'r.csv' on customerId;
from 'orders.csv' | join (from 'r.csv' | where qty > 1) on customerId;
from 'orders.csv' | join 'r.csv' on customerId, amount
---- expected
info[DS1007]: `join` renamed 2 columns of the right table: `amount` to `amount1`, `qty` to `qty2`
  --> query:1:26
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | join 'r.csv' on customerId;
  |                          ^^^^^^^ this table has columns with the same names as the left side
  |
  = help: to choose the names yourself, rename them on the right: `join (from 'r.csv' | project-rename right_amount = amount, right_qty = qty)`
  = note: a column named in `on` is not renamed: the two sides make one column (only `$left.a == $right.b` keeps both)

info[DS1007]: `join` renamed 2 columns of the right table: `amount` to `amount1`, `qty` to `qty2`
  --> query:2:26
  |
2 | from 'orders.csv' | join (from 'r.csv' | where qty > 1) on customerId;
  |                          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this table has columns with the same names as the left side
  |
  = help: to choose the names yourself, rename them on the right: `join (from 'r.csv' | where qty > 1 | project-rename right_amount = amount, right_qty = qty)`
  = note: a column named in `on` is not renamed: the two sides make one column (only `$left.a == $right.b` keeps both)

info[DS1007]: `join` renamed column `qty` of the right table to `qty2`
  --> query:3:26
  |
3 | from 'orders.csv' | join 'r.csv' on customerId, amount
  |                          ^^^^^^^ this table also has a column `qty`
  |
  = help: to choose the names yourself, rename them on the right: `join (from 'r.csv' | project-rename right_qty = qty)`
  = note: a column named in `on` is not renamed: the two sides make one column (only `$left.a == $right.b` keeps both)

